WHAT THIS COVERS

Ground-truth files, dataset manifests, datasheets, policy packs, transcripts,
audio specifications and audio manifests, labelling guides and label files,
the Day-60 rubric and scoresheet, and everything under `results/`.

WHAT IT DOES NOT COVER

The code, which is MIT. See `LICENSE`.

The private splits. They are not published, are not in this repository, and
are not licensed to anyone. They exist to detect tuning against the public
sets.

NOTE ON THE DATA ITSELF

Every item is synthetic. Nothing was scraped, nothing was copied from a real
document, and no real invoice, statement, claim form, transcript or recording
entered any set. Identifiers that resemble government or financial identifiers
are format-valid and checksum-invalid by construction, so that nothing here
can resolve to a real person or account.

Charter section 6, in `charter/methodology.md`, governs how the data was made
and what it is not suitable for.
